It is wonderfully sunny now.
The good weather makes me very cheerful.
Next to the water, I see a small bakery.
I go inside.
A friendly woman stands behind the counter.
"Good afternoon," she says.
"Good afternoon," I answer.
"I would like a coffee and a piece of cake, please."
"With pleasure," the shop assistant says.
She gives me the coffee and the cake.
"That makes five euros and eighty cents," she says.
I give her the money.
"Do you need the receipt?" she asks.
"No, thank you," I say.
I take my snack in my hand.
I go back outside to the canal.
The sky is radiantly blue.
It will stay sunny today.
